<body>
    <h1>Product Branching (Quantity &gt;1 create multiple line items and ha=
rdware)</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <div class=3D"panel" style=3D"background-color: #EAE6FF;border-colo=
r: #998DD9;border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"panelContent" style=3D"background-color: #EAE6FF;">
<p>Fortra Reviewed 12.1.2025</p>
</div>
</div>
<p>Power Branching =E2=80=93 Salesforce&nbsp;</p>
<p>The following two order line branching models are required in Fortra Sal=
esforce. The branching model used will be defined at the SKU level and that=
 SKU will be treated the same way each time it appears on an order.&nbsp;&n=
bsp;&nbsp;</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Branch Type: =E2=80=9COrder Line Only=E2=80=9D&nbsp;</p></li>
</ol>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Order lines cloned when quantity is &gt; 1.&nbsp;</p></li>
</ol>
<ol start=3D"2">
<li>
<p>Manual discount amount is divided evenly across all cloned lines.&nbsp;&=
nbsp;</p></li>
</ol>
<ol start=3D"3">
<li>
<p>Displaced ARR is divided evenly across all cloned lines.&nbsp;</p></li>
</ol>
<ol start=3D"4">
<li>
<p>Hardware not cloned =E2=80=93 All cloned order lines are linked to the o=
ne original hardware record&nbsp;</p></li>
</ol>
<ol start=3D"5">
<li>
<p>Partitions are cloned =E2=80=93 Each cloned order line has its own clone=
d partition all linked to the one original hardware record&nbsp;</p></li>
</ol>
<ol start=3D"6">
<li>
<p>Example: Order Line with quantity =3D 4&nbsp;</p></li>
</ol>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>One order line with quantity 4 becomes four order lines each with quanti=
ty 1&nbsp;</p></li>
</ol>
<ol start=3D"2">
<li>
<p>If the original order line has a partition the partition is also cloned,=
 and each order line has its own unique partition&nbsp;</p></li>
</ol>
<ol start=3D"3">
<li>
<p>All 4 order lines and their partitions are linked to the one original ha=
rdware record&nbsp;</p></li>
</ol>
<ol start=3D"4">
<li>
<p>1 order line, 1 partition, 1 hardware record (4 total records) becomes 4=
 order lines, 4 partitions, 1 hardware record (9 total records)&nbsp;</p></=
li>
</ol>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<ol start=3D"2">
<li>
<p>Branch Type: =E2=80=9COrder Line and Hardware=E2=80=9D&nbsp;</p></li>
</ol>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Order lines cloned when quantity is &gt; 1.&nbsp;</p></li>
</ol>
<ol start=3D"2">
<li>
<p>Manual discount amount is divided evenly across all cloned lines.&nbsp;&=
nbsp;</p></li>
</ol>
<ol start=3D"3">
<li>
<p>Displaced ARR is divided evenly across all cloned lines.&nbsp;</p></li>
</ol>
<ol start=3D"4">
<li>
<p>Hardware is cloned =E2=80=93 Each cloned order line has its own cloned h=
ardware record&nbsp;</p></li>
</ol>
<ol start=3D"5">
<li>
<p>Partitions are cloned =E2=80=93 Each cloned order line has its own parti=
tion linked to its hardware record&nbsp;</p></li>
</ol>
<ol start=3D"6">
<li>
<p>Example: Order Line with quantity =3D 3&nbsp;</p></li>
</ol>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>One order line with quantity 3 becomes 3 order lines each with quantity =
1&nbsp;</p></li>
</ol>
<ol start=3D"2">
<li>
<p>If the original order line has a partition the partition is also cloned,=
 and each order line has its own unique partition&nbsp;</p></li>
</ol>
<ol start=3D"3">
<li>
<p>If the original order line has a hardware record the hardware is also cl=
oned, and each order line and partition have their own unique hardware reco=
rd.&nbsp;</p></li>
</ol>
<ol start=3D"4">
<li>
<p>1 order line, 1 partition, 1 hardware record (3 total records) becomes 3=
 order lines, 3 partitions, 3 hardware records. (9 total records)&nbsp;</p>=
</li>
</ol>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
